    "function_valuation": "With t=1/x, y=epsilon*t^-3*(1+(A/2)*t^4+(B/2)*t^6+...). For v=sum(v_i*x^i), first nonzero Laurent coefficient of y-v gives signed ord at each epsilon=+/-1. Generic v3 unequal +/-1 has ord=-3 at both; if epsilon=v3 and v2!=0 ord=-2, else v1!=0 ord=-1, else v0!=0 ord=0, else A!=0 ord=+1. Retain zeros as well as poles. Finite divisor has roots of f-v^2 with multiplicity and y=v; norm its full signed divisor including infinity.",
